Translate Express does not collect any data and has no server of its own.

Translation is done by third-party services, which may collect some data to improve their services:
- Google Translate, by default.
- Groq, only if you paste your own API key in the extension settings. The text to translate is then sent to Groq. The key is stored only in the extension's local storage in your browser and is sent only to Groq.

The API key is stored in clear in the extension's local storage in your browser (an extension cannot encrypt a secret in a useful way). It is never available to web pages and is only sent to the provider over HTTPS.

The diagnostics log (events, durations, token counts, short examples of untranslated text) stays in your browser's session storage and is never sent anywhere. You can clear it from the dashboard or turn it off with the "diagnostics" setting.

Translate Express is a fork of TWP - Translate Web Pages: https://github.com/FilipePS/Traduzir-paginas-web
